# lane.env — this recipe's serving constants (the control surface's only inputs).
#
# Sourced by bin/start.sh, bin/stop.sh and site/preflight wrapper. Everything a lane switch
# needs to know about THIS recipe is here; nothing in bin/ reads a sibling recipe.
#
# The vendored upstream tree (upstream/) carries its own config/cluster.json; this file is
# what makes the spark-recipes control surface agree with it. If they disagree, `doctor`
# does not catch it (it validates cluster.json) — hence DRIFT_CHECK below, run by
# bin/start.sh --dry-run and by bin/stop.sh.

# --- identity -----------------------------------------------------------------------
LANE_LABEL="dsv41f-vllm-lane"
PIN="d3d40d94"                       # tag spark-ds41f-1120 -> d3d40d941f2752fea95aa770eb10d41b5ad5aa1a
PIN_TAG="spark-ds41f-1120"
UPSTREAM_SLUG="christopherowen/spark-ds41f"

# --- paths (identical on every node; the recipe rides the shared repo checkout) -------
# HOME is normally set; derive it from the passwd entry when it is not (a non-login shell or
# a dry run from a harness that does not export it), so --dry-run works anywhere.
if [ -z "${HOME:-}" ]; then
  HOME=$(getent passwd "$(id -un)" 2>/dev/null | cut -d: -f6)
  [ -n "$HOME" ] || HOME=$PWD
fi
# DEPLOY_PATH may be exported to point a dry run / drill at a staged copy. Never set it for a
# real start: bin/start.sh asserts it matches the vendored cluster.json's deployment.path suffix.
: "${DEPLOY_PATH:=$HOME/code/spark-recipes/deepseek-v41-flash-christopherowen/upstream}"
CONFIG_REL="config/cluster.json"

# --- serving ------------------------------------------------------------------------
SERVED_NAME="deepseek-v41-flash"
IMAGE="spark-ds41f:1120"
SHAPE="tp4-ring-4k"
SHAPE_UNQUALIFIED=1                  # no benchmark_reference until P2-7 promotes a run

# --- container (ONE name on all four nodes — upstream's design, not per-rank) --------
CONTAINER_NAMES="spark-ds41f"

# --- image identity: the five tree labels the release lock expects --------------------
EXPECTED_LABELS="\
local.spark-ds41f.vllm.tree=8fc99ca7546c5c538f0fe64e7c82954f1d2d7ae0 \
local.spark-ds41f.nccl.tree=6af10aa730a64fcee8781d62340a9c9184e79469 \
local.spark-ds41f.tilelang.tree=741806c7357102130a149cdcae2a5f22678eab67 \
local.spark-ds41f.tile_kernels.tree=cb2fa41c8af290204c81c547ed678ebf957cca53 \
local.spark-ds41f.sparknet.tree=e06f6a0675cb66638231d2c68948a2b315b69b07"

# --- host contract deltas this lane carries (documented, not enforced) ---------------
# NCCL_IB_MERGE_NICS=1 in the vendored cluster.json is INERT here: our ring map gives each
# neighbour exactly ONE HCA (2-PF subset), and merge only applies to >=2 stripes per link.
# Upstream's example map uses two stripes (both PCIe roots) and needs the merge. Do not
# "fix" this to 0 without also changing the node map and measuring — see research.md D6.
# NCCL_SWITCHLESS_BIDIRECTIONAL=2 is upstream's shipped default; the P2-6 A/B measures it.
LANE_NCCL="libnccl from the image (not the host four-PF lib); 2-PF subset per neighbour"